  "imageName": "arrow.right.circle.fill",
  "intro": "The dative case answers Кому? Чему? (To whom? To what?). It's the case of the RECIPIENT - the person who receives something. Use it for indirect objects (Дай мне книгу - Give me the book), with verbs like звонить (call), помогать (help), and in impersonal constructions expressing feelings or necessity (Мне холодно - I'm cold, Мне нужно - I need).",
  "rules": [
    "Dative answers Кому? Чему? (To whom? To what?) - marks the recipient or beneficiary.",
    "Dative answers 'to whom?' or 'for whom?': дал книгу другу (gave book to friend).",
    "Used with age expressions: мне двадцать лет (I am twenty years old).",
    "Used with нравиться: мне нравится (I like, lit. 'to me it pleases').",
    "Verbs requiring dative: помогать (help), звонить (call), советовать (advise)."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Дай мне книгу. (Give me the book.), мне = dative of я",
    "Я звоню брату. (I'm calling my brother.), звонить + dative",
    "Мне холодно. (I'm cold.), impersonal + dative",
    "Помоги маме! (Help mom!), помогать + dative"
  ],
